! The Fermi-Dirac twin of h-chain-spiral-elk.in, and the cell to prefer for any
! new spiral comparison against Elk.
!
! **It differs in one word, and that word is why the pair exists.** Elk computes
! its entropy term only for Fermi-Dirac smearing (energy.f90:242,
! IF (stype == 3)), so with the Gaussian its total is an INTERNAL energy where
! this code's and QE's are FREE energies, and E(q) - E(0) means a different thing
! on the two sides. At degauss = 0.1 Ry that gap is 112 meV between q = 0 and
! q = 1/4, five times the difference being compared, and it is the whole of the
! factor of five PLAN.md P86 could not place and P105 resolved. With fermi-dirac
! on this side and stype = 3 on Elk's, both totals carry -TS and the two can be
! subtracted directly.
!
! degauss is unchanged at 0.1 Ry: for this scheme it is kT, and Elk's swidth is
! kT in Hartree, so 0.1 Ry against 0.05 Ha is the same pair of numbers the
! Gaussian fixture already carried.
!
! **The state is not the Gaussian cell's and no number should be carried across.**
! A different smearing function is a different free-energy surface, so the moment,
! the energy and E(q) - E(0) all move; what this fixture buys is that the two
! codes are on the same surface as each other, which the other pair was not.
!
! The QE-side twin of tests/data/elk/h_chain_spiral/elk.in: the SAME hydrogen
! chain spiral, set up so that the two codes differ by their basis and nothing
! else that can be helped.
!
! One line differs from h-chain-spiral.in and it is input_dft. Elk's Perdew-
! Zunger LDA (xctype = 2) is implemented spin-unpolarised only and Elk refuses a
! magnetic run with it, so the functional both codes can do is Perdew-Wang
! (Elk's default xctype = 3, QE's 'pw'). The dataset is still H.pz-vbc.UPF, a
! PZ-generated pseudopotential run under PW -- an inconsistency that exists on
! the QE side alone, Elk being all-electron, and one hydrogen tolerates because
! it has no core.
!
! Also changed: conv_thr and the spiral wavevector are left where the scan sets
! them, and degauss stays at 0.1 Ry (Elk's swidth = 0.05 Ha) for the reason the
! original header gives -- at a small smearing this soft magnetic surface lands
! in whichever nearby minimum the starting density is closest to.
!
! PLAN.md P86 has the comparison.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 0.41666666666667,
    nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    input_dft = 'pw'
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'fermi-dirac', degauss = 0.10
    noncolin = .true.
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6
    angle1(1) = 90.0
    spiral_q(1) = 0.0, spiral_q(2) = 0.0, spiral_q(3) = 0.25
    nbnd = 6
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 4 0 0 0
